  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Climber’s Logbook",
    "overview": "The owner approved the design review on 31 October 2026 and directed all work to this Expo app. The old Next.js repository is deprecated. Visual source: https://bouldy-design-review.elatedbread66.chatgpt.site and the sibling `bouldy-design-review/components/design-review` source. This supersedes the previous one-for-one visual migration restriction. Domain/authentication/privacy safeguards remain unchanged.\n\nSource snapshot: `55b51d8` (31 October 2026). The structured tokens below describe shared primitives; page-specific values such as the profile hero’s larger corners and PageTitle’s compressed heading metrics are intentional exceptions. Preview ramps are generated documentation aids, not extra runtime colours. The original migration screenshots and earlier 78-test evidence do not verify this entire current design.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Approved cream/limestone surfaces with shared climbing identity.",
      "Four main tabs; catalogue management is an administrator destination.",
      "Native edge-to-edge frames with a centred browser phone canvas.",
      "Explicit section/action error recovery and page-matched cold skeletons."
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the approved cream/limestone identity, supplied fonts and brand artwork.",
      "**Do** fill the native device width while preserving the browser phone canvas.",
      "**Do** use shared controls, explicit error recovery, account-safe state and reduced motion.",
      "**Do** record exact commits and platforms when accepting behaviour."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** revert to the old five-tab or exact-copy visual baseline.",
      "**Don't** invent activity, timing, admin authority or offline persistence.",
      "**Don't** treat screenshots, previews or a source commit as full device/PWA/release acceptance."
    ]
  }
}
